- lib/overview.js: per event, web = a real listener of that DOM type (the probe
  now answers listenersAll), or the wire field map, or only a mention; C++ port =
  SourceTree.defState(): live / only in #if 0 / only in a comment / none (stops
  at the first live definition, so a 2,900-control page takes ~30 ms); BCB6 too
- overview tab: summary chips, filters (web not wired / no same-name C++ /
  controls not on the page), text filter; click a row -> designer selects it,
  click a location -> opens it. The C++ column is labelled for what it is: a
  same-name TfXxx:: function -- web pages often go through commands instead
- test\panels_render.ps1: the properties panel and the overview drawn in a
  headless Edge with the real data of the fake-vscode layer (no JS error, the
  right sections and rows, double-click / click post the right messages)

Tests: lib 68 / probe 2 pages / fake vscode 43 + panels 8 / real VS Code 42
incl. an 8-page sweep that also runs the overview -- all pass, 12 opened files
byte-identical (MD5).

